# Windows batch files MUST keep CRLF line endings and stay ASCII.
# Git's default normalisation would otherwise convert them to LF on clone
# (or on a Linux checkout), and cmd.exe then mis-parses every line:
#   'LOID6' is not recognized as an internal or external command
# That failure looks like a code bug but is purely a line-ending problem.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Fonts / binaries - never touch
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.dll binary
*.pdf binary
